Source-count vs built-count (A9.3): columns 2 · dots 36+1=37 · ratio labels 2 · arrows 2 — Execute prints these against the CONFIG census and halts on mismatch.

### P2. Construction choice
**Chosen: DOM + inline SVG in one self-contained HTML file** — columns as DOM blocks (reserved label band + board area), dots as SVG circles (or DOM divs) generated from `columns[]`, arrows as SVG paths with stroke-dash draw-on, population count-up as a rAF-driven CONFIG clock, one phase machine sequencing: tiles-in → count-ups → cascade (per column, in CONFIG order) → placeholder morph → paired hold → annotation draw → final hold. Rejected alternatives, one line each:
- Canvas particle system — rejected: no particle field exists (O6/A5); canvas would re-import the convergent-freeze failure class for zero mechanical gain and weaken per-dot DOM state probes (A11 assertions read dot states directly).
- CSS keyframes only — rejected: counts/cardinality are data-driven (36 generated dots, derived ratios); keyframes would hardcode the specimen's timeline as literals, violating §2.1/A9.6.
- Video/frame-sequence or traced silhouettes — rejected: refusal-class (§6.1); silhouettes are code-drawn simplified paths from CONFIG tokens.
- Full SVG-only scene — rejected: label-band fit measurement and count-up text are DOM-native in the family's proven builds (T53/T82); SVG text fit is the weaker instrument here.

Sequencing by construction (Cure-2 translation): the phase machine advances a column's cascade only when the prior column's settle completes; annotation phase is gated on all columns settled — overlap is unrepresentable, not merely unscheduled.

### P3. Schedule basis + census-anchor mapping (A7 / A10.2)
**Window-scope line: schedule basis = `segment-anchored`.** Segment = source **83.5–102.5 s** (duration **19.0 s** to cut, §3 step 1); build clock `buildMs = (sourceT − 84.0) × 1000 + 500` (the 500 ms handle shows the prior scene's last beat, then the transition). All phases sit at their measured segment times; nothing is re-based.
| CP | Census state (source t) | Segment-relative ms | Prescribed state at that instant (CONFIG-derived) |
|---|---|---|---|
| CP1 | 85.5 TX alone, pop counting | 2000 | column[0] tile at full ink; population display strictly between 0 and 25,268,000; column[1] absent |
| CP2 | 89.5 both tiles, pops complete | 6000 | both populations at full CONFIG values; zero dots landed |
| CP3 | 90.5 cascade mid-flight | 7000 | TX dots landed count in (0,36); TX tile opacity < 0.5; VT dot count = 0 |
| CP4 | 91.5 TX grid complete | 8000 | TX dots = 36; TX tile opacity = 0; VT dots = 0 (zero-state anchor — guards.md #8 probe applies) |
| CP5 | 95.0 VT dot present | 11500 | VT dots = 1; TX dots = 36; no ratio labels visible |
| CP6 | 98.0 arrows drawing | 14500 | both ratio labels visible with derived values 702,000 / 630,000; at least one arrow dash-offset strictly between 0 and full |
| CP7 | 100.5 final state | 17000 | arrows complete; full paired state holds |
**Departure table (A10.2):** (1) Catalogue window ends 111 s; the prescribed segment ends 102.5 s — departure reason: census frames 104–110 s show T209's square morph + +2 dots, a different technique (not owed); including them would build T209 inside T208 (§8 size discipline). (2) Digest prose says dots land "in grids timed to the spoken count" without separating the tile-staging beat (84.5–89.5); the Plan includes the tile beat because the census shows the dots land OVER the dissolving tiles — omitting it would misstate the motion the motion lens prices.

### P4. Swap design (exact altered values)
Content swap: columns → [{label:'Alpha', population:1200000, count:12, gridCols:4, tile silhouette:'none'}, {label:'Beta', population:300000, count:3, gridCols:3, tile silhouette:'none'}] — derived ratios must read 100,000 / 100,000; dot totals 12 / 3 by CONFIG census. Timing swap (one): `cascadeMs × 1.5` via CONFIG (A11 assertion instants for CP3/CP4 must move by the same CONFIG expression — receipt shows the changed evaluation instant, A12). Palette swap (one): `palette.arrow` '#5b84ae' → '#c2543a' and `palette.ink` '#111111' → '#1d3a6e' is TWO values — palette leg uses arrow only: '#c2543a'. Pass = technique still reads (paired counts land in order, ratios derived correctly, annotation draws) under all three swaps.

### P5. Execute + Verify checklists (instruments)
**Execute:** E1 cut segment 83.5–102.5 s → `segment.mp4`, ffprobe facts filed vs guards.md #5 · E2 build `recreation.html` (CONFIG-first, §P2 construction, no literals in animation logic) · E3 source-vs-built count print (A9.3: 2 / 37 / 2 / 2) · E4 build `comparison.html` (shared controls, labels, phone stacking) · E5 own-checks with RAW output filed from first draft (A9.4): purity grep · swap harness · syntax + seeded-RNG census · census-anchor probes incl. CP4 zero-state (guards.md #8) · E6 A6 legs filed (`fit-table.md` — reserved-band rows: name/population/ratio measured post-fit ink at 360 px, floor ~11 px, instrument = harness post-fit measurement or named stand-in font per A12.2, never a character-width model · `config-census.md` — every §P1 key resolved to an application site, nested `columns[]` keys included) · E7 A11 assertions CP1–CP7 each with CONFIG expression + evaluation instant + A12 executable receipt (command, expression, raw result) · E8 A13 RECEIPT INDEX reconciled (guards.md commands 1–8 applicability + all A11 assertions; every line a receipt or a NOT-DEMANDED line with governing citation).
**Verify:** V1 swap test (guards.md #2) on §P4 exact values, raw output filed · V2 purity grep (guards.md #1; specimen alternatives incl. `ajavsMbCapY`-form ids; `url(#id)` fragments classified, not counted) · V3 comparison check (both sides play from shared control; durations matched 19.0 s; labels; phone stacking) · V4 **jev-prewave call point** — after legs 1–3 + A6 legs + receipt-index reconciliation, payload carries both A6 outputs verbatim (A10.1); HOLD returns build to Execute, wave not spent · V5 **five-lens scoring wave** (motion · timing · purity · reusability · readability), five separate score-blind runs, returns filed verbatim under `codex/` before any arithmetic · V6 consolidation (guards.md #4): average ≥85 AND min ≥70, arithmetic shown, no rounding up.

### P6. Failure-point evaluation (priced from this job's record)
- **Convergent freeze** — the T15 class (formed state static while surplus freezes): LOW here by construction — no particle pool, nothing moves except scheduled landings; the priced residue is the opposite defect, a cascade that reads as a fade (T82 motion 80) — cured by per-dot settle (scale+ink) in CONFIG, priced under motion.
- **Intensity collapse** — dots vs faded tile: census shows dots land over a tile still mid-fade at 90.5 (tile ≈50% grey behind black dots reads cleanly); risk is a build that fades the tile too slowly so early dots sit on dark tile and vanish — `tileFadeMs` is CONFIG and CP3 asserts tile opacity <0.5 mid-cascade.
- **Overlap** — phase overlap (Cure-2 class): TX cascade vs VT landing vs annotation — excluded by the phase machine (P2), and CP4/CP5 assert the separations mechanically.
- **Fitting limits** — ratio figures + arrows occupy the centre band between columns; at 360 px the 702,000/630,000 labels and arrow curves can collide with the TX grid's right edge — reserved annotation band + fit-table rows for both ratio labels are the instrument; population lines (25,268,000) are the widest label-band rows and are measured, not assumed.
- **Render-proof limitation** — PIXEL-UNVERIFIED stands (no browser binary in this seat, family precedent T53/T82/T45): fit evidence is harness post-fit ink measurement; lens verdicts are source-based; the comparison page is the render surface. Printed, not hidden.

### P7. Plateau priced (A2 — before Execute)
Family average **87.0** (O5); bar 85 / floor 70. Predicted minimum lens: **reusability** — it is the family minimum in T53 (74) and T45 (78) and joint-minimum in T82 (80), and T208's reusability surface is exactly the family's failure shape (array cardinality, derived-vs-literal ratios, override semantics). Stuck-lens hypothesis: IF reusability sticks, the cause will be `columns[]` handling — a build that special-cases two columns or literals the derived ratio — not the dot mechanics; the Plan's cures (array-generated columns, `ratioMode:'derived'`, wholesale array replacement on override) are aimed there in advance. Secondary risk: timing — the VT morph is bracketed to ≈93.7–94.5 by the supplementary census (mid-morph at 94.0, complete at 94.5); the Plan anchors the morph START to the spoken "one" (93.71 s → segment-relative 10210 ms, `placeholderMorphMs` 600 completing ≈94.3, inside the bracket) and the timing lens prices that allocation against the bracket, not against a fabricated frame-exact instant. If this attempt averages ≤87.0 without passing, scores.md carries the A2 WHY naming the stuck lens against this prediction.

### P8. Codex call dispositions
- **codex-observe:** **CONFIRMED-WITH-GAPS** (3 findings) — return filed verbatim as `item-T208-codex-observe-return.md`; full disposition in §O6 (all three applied/confirmed; finding 3's residual unknowns closed firsthand by supplementary census frames 20–22).
- **codex-plan-review:** **REVISE** (5 findings) — return filed verbatim as `item-T208-codex-plan-review-return.md`; disposition: ALL FIVE APPLIED as the binding Plan amendments in §P9 below (construction suitable per the return; the REVISE prices schedule authority, contrast, and cardinality-swap gaps, each cured in the Plan text before Execute — advisory verdict consumed by application, per the 2026-11-14 ruling).

### Gaps stated plainly
G1. VT dot morph known to the ≈93.7–94.5 bracket after the supplementary census (was 93.5–95.0); priced in P7, not fabricated finer than that. G2. Population count-up easing (linear vs stepped) not resolvable from 1.5 s census frames — Plan treats it as CONFIG (`countUpMs`) with linear default; a motion-lens finding, if any, prices it at Verify. G3. No prior attempt exists for T208 itself — family pricing rests on siblings, named as such. G4. Silhouette shapes are simplified code-drawn paths by design (purity), so tile-stage visual fidelity is approximate — the technique priced is the dot count, not the cartography.

### P9. Plan amendments on codex-plan-review REVISE (applied, binding on Execute)
- **R1 (finding 1 — landing geometry):** each dot's landing carries a nonzero geometric change, not opacity alone: CONFIG `dotLandScaleFrom:1.6` + `dotLandDy:-8` (stage px, settles to 0 over `dotSettleMs`). CP3 additionally asserts at least one dot IN FLIGHT (scale strictly between 1 and 1.6) and at least one SETTLED at the same instant.
- **R2 (finding 2 — contrast + exclusivity compiled):** (a) dots and tiles render on SEPARATE layers; a dot's first visibility is bound to the contrast condition — tile opacity at that dot's position ≤ `tileContrastGate:0.55` — and the own-checks probe the EARLIEST landing (first dot) against its composited backing as well as CP3. (b) Each column carries explicit CONFIG events `events:{entranceMs, countUpStartMs, revealMode:'cascade'|'morph', revealAnchorMs}` (defaults from the census/narration anchors: TX entrance 500 · count-up 1050 · cascade anchor 5430 [= spoken "36" 90.43 s]; VT entrance 3630 · count-up 3630 · morph anchor 10210 [= spoken "one" 93.71 s]); Vermont has exactly ONE reveal event (the morph) — no generic cascade path exists for a `revealMode:'morph'` column. (c) ONE compiled schedule is derived from CONFIG + predecessor completion and drives rendering, seek, and checkpoint evaluation alike; an anchor that precedes its dependency's completion is CLAMPED to that completion (start = max(anchor, predecessor-complete)) — this rule is also how the timing swap behaves (§P4's ×1.5 cascade moves CP3/CP4 instants through the same compiled schedule). (d) Assertions added: zero VT round dots through TX settle (CP4 form) · zero annotation elements until all reveals settle AND the paired hold completes (CP5/CP6 boundary).
- **R3 (finding 3 — parameterization completion):** §P1 gains: `columns[].events` (above) · `columns[].x / boardTop` (column placement + vertical rhythm) · `ratioLabelDx/Dy` + `arrowCurve` (annotation placement/curvature) · `personGlyph:true`. **`cascadeMs` is the authoritative landing window**: `dotStaggerMs` is DERIVED, never set independently — stagger = (cascadeMs − dotSettleMs) / max(count−1, 1); single-dot columns take stagger 0 and their reveal is the morph/settle rule, not a cascade. (Check on defaults: cascade 2000 ms, settle 220 → stagger ≈ 50.9 ms for 36 dots; the §P4 timing swap ×1.5 therefore provably moves the completion span.) Swap extended: the §P4 content swap is joined by a **1-column variant** (Alpha only) and a **3-column variant** (Alpha 12 / Beta 3 / Gamma 5, gridCols 4/3/3), each asserting event order, generated dot totals, derived ratios, and no layout collision in the reserved bands. CP1–CP7 assertions are evaluated against the CONFIGURED columns/events (the specimen values in §P3 are the default-configuration expectations, not hardcoded test constants).
- **R4 (finding 4 — bar arithmetic):** CONFIRMED, no change to the prediction (reusability minimum; family benchmark 87.0). One correction of form adopted: A2's mandatory WHY binds a re-attempt against the technique's OWN prior average; T208 has no prior attempt (G3), so §P7's plateau text stands as a prediction + benchmark, and the WHY obligation would attach to any SECOND attempt against this attempt's filed average.
- **R5 (finding 5 — handles scoped):** the recreation's display during the handles is now prescribed: opening handle (build 0–500 ms) = the empty paper stage with texture only (the prior Capitol scene is NOT recreated); closing handle (after CP7, to segment end 102.5 s) = the final paired state HOLDING (the T209 square morph is NOT recreated). The 19.0 s window stands for comparison sync only.
