**Motion findings (A10.3 form):** motion instants = 84.5–85.5 (scene transition in) · 85.5–87.0 (TX population count-up) · 87.0–88.5 (VT column entrance + count-up) · 89.4–91.5 (Texas dot cascade, column-wise, tile cross-dissolves under it) · 93.5–95.0 (Vermont square→dot) · 96.5–99.5 (ratio numbers + arrows draw-on). Holds = 91.5–93.5 partial (TX settled, VT pending) · 95.0–96.5 full paired hold (≈1.5 s+) · 100.5–102.0 final hold (≥1.5 s). Dissolves = the state tiles cross-fade OUT as their dots land (tile is a staging surface, never co-present at full strength with the completed grid); the whole board exits by transition at 102–104 into T209 (not recreated — T209 is a separate, not-owed technique).

**Spoken-count pricing (words data, `asr-segments.json` in the digest dir — the technique is timed to the count):**
- "Texas" first named 85.05 s; TX population narration runs 85.63–87.03 ("which has a huge population") — census: TX count-up completes inside this span ✓.
- "Vermont" named 87.63 s; VT sentence ends 89.19 s — census: VT column + count-up inside this span ✓.
- **"Texas has 36 representatives in Congress"** — words: "Texas" 89.43 · "36" **90.43** · "representatives" 90.83 · segment ends 92.21. Census: the 36-dot cascade runs 89.5–91.5, i.e. it brackets the spoken "36" — dots land WITH the count sentence, completing ≈0.7 s after "representatives" lands. The cascade is the visual form of this sentence.
- **"Vermont only gets one"** — "Vermont" 92.81 · "one" **93.71** · segment ends 94.17. Census: VT still a square at 93.5, round dot by 95.0 — the single dot lands on/just after "one" (94.17–95.0 bracket; finer landing instant is sub-census-resolution, priced as a gap in §P7).
- "Representatives in both states each represent roughly the same number of people" 94.81–98.89 — census: paired hold then ratio arrows draw across 96.5–99.5, completing as the sentence ends; the arrows ARE this sentence's visual.

### O3. Variables (§1.3 — every property that can change without changing the technique)
1. Column count (2) and column identities/labels (Texas/Vermont). 2. Per-column population values + their count-up duration. 3. Per-column dot counts (36 / 1). 4. Grid geometry: columns-per-grid (6), dot radius, dot gap, fill order (column-wise), per-dot stagger, dot settle/fade duration. 5. Tile layer: tile size per column, silhouette on/off + which silhouette, tile fade duration. 6. Vermont placeholder form (square→dot morph duration). 7. Ratio values (702,000 / 630,000), ratio label position, arrow colour/curvature/draw duration. 8. Palette: background (paper white), dot ink (black), tile grey, arrow blue, text ink. 9. Type: name size, population size, ratio size, person-glyph on/off. 10. All beat timings (entrances, count-ups, cascade window, holds, annotation window). 11. Stage size / column x-positions / vertical rhythm. 12. Background texture (faint newsprint) on/off + opacity. Each becomes a CONFIG key in §P1.

### O4. Consumer
**Diagram containers — the DLC assembler's count-board surface.** Reason: the assembler's count boards must show a count as accumulated physical units whose fullness IS the result (the T53/T82 family form); T208 adds the PAIRED form — two counts at two scales on one stage with a derived per-unit ratio annotated — which is exactly the shape a "fair stage before the distortion" beat needs in explainer diagrams (compare two groups, land each count on its spoken beat, then annotate the per-unit value). Secondary: explainer production diagram container generally. The technique's text (names, populations, ratios) IS the subject, not captions (§6.5).

### O5. Prior / family scores read (filed scores.md lens lines)
- **T53 ballot-arc count board — PASS 85.6** (motion 92 · timing 88 · purity 94 · reusability **74** · readability 80; min 74). Prices: count-board reusability is the family's weak lens — bracket/threshold derivations and array-cardinality overrides were its named defects; T208's Plan must derive ratio labels from population÷count (not literals) and support cardinality change.
- **T82 countable multitude — PASS 87.2** (motion 80 · timing 89 · purity 100 · reusability 80 · readability 87; min 80). Prices: a pure DOM/canvas dot multitude reaches purity 100 and timing 89 when landings sit on measured anchors; motion was its joint-minimum (80) — dot landings must read as landings, not fades-only.
- **T45 number-anchored beats — PASS 88.2** (motion 88 · timing 84 · purity 97 · reusability **78** · readability 94; min 78). Prices: number-anchored timing holds up when beats sit on the spoken numbers; reusability again the minimum (fixed cardinality of exactly two panels was its defect) — T208's two-column form must NOT hardcode two.
- Family average (3 siblings, 5-lens): (85.6 + 87.2 + 88.2) / 3 = **87.0**. Family minimum-lens pattern: reusability is the minimum in 2 of 3 (74, 78) and joint-minimum in the third (80).

### O6. Standing-guidance dispositions (A9.5 — reasoning inline at this gate)
- **A1.2 runtime text sampling — NOT-BINDING.** That precedent governs typography constructions whose letterforms are BUILT by sampling config-rendered text (particle typography, T15). T208's text is ordinary typeset labels (names, populations, ratios) and its marks are geometric dots on a grid — no letterform is sampled, formed, or dissolved. Binding it would import a construction the technique does not contain.
- **A5 flow-field model + Owner Cures 1–2 — NOT-BINDING as a construction; Cure 2's principle binds in translated form.** There is no particle field: dots are discrete counted units that land once and hold; there is no stream to borrow from, no reserve fraction, and no velocity to keep continuous — the flow-field model has no object here. Owner Cure 1 (fg/bg intensity separation) has no field to separate against; the census shows the one separation that exists — black dots at full ink over a tile that has faded to light grey — and that is priced as the tile-fade variable, not a borrow flag. Owner Cure 2 (strict sequencing, one lifecycle owns the stage) DOES bind as a sequencing principle, translated: the census shows Texas's cascade completes before Vermont's dot lands, and the ratio annotation begins only after both counts settle — the Plan's phase machine enforces that order by construction (§P2).
- **A9.1 plate construction — BINDS in its still-plate branch.** The background is a faint static newsprint texture: it never moves in any census frame. Any background motion would exceed the technique, so the Plan prices a STILL plate (texture as a CONFIG-controlled static layer, opacity key) and no pan/wrap/tiling machinery is built. The dark state TILES under each column are not a background plate — they are per-column staging surfaces that dissolve; they are priced as subject elements (§P1), not under A9.1.
- **Reserved-band badge note (HQ board `practice-2026-11-18-t06-construction-note`) — BINDS.** T208's labels (column names, population lines, ratio numbers) sit in fixed bands above/inside a board whose grid area scales with the container in the DLC count-board surface; under the note, labels that scale with a container get a reserved band with legibility floors instead of scaling with it. The Plan therefore reserves a fixed label band per column (names + population) and a fixed annotation band for the ratio figures, with measured-fit floors (§P5), rather than letting type shrink with the board.
- **A9.6 parameterization depth — BINDS:** every subject-shaping value (counts, grid geometry, tile geometry, arrow geometry, all timings) is CONFIG data in §P1.
- **A11 census checkpoints — BINDS:** checkpoints CP1–CP7 in §P3 each map to an executable assertion with a CONFIG-derived evaluation instant in the Verify checklist (§P5).

