../../INSTRUCTION.md:104:## Amendment A7 (2026-11-15, Cycle 013 Condense — pattern rule fired: T64 + T66 timing lenses)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:105:**Schedule basis is a required Plan field.** The §9 pattern rule fired this cycle: two techniques' timing lenses independently priced the same defect class — a recreation whose schedule is silently re-based from the segment's measured timeline (T64 lens-timing −16: calendar entrances at 0.4/1.4 s vs measured ~4/5 s · T66 lens-timing-interim1 −18: opening state mismatching the measured window). Standing requirement, binding on every Plan from Wave 12 onward: each item's window-scope line in the wave RUN.md names its **schedule basis** — `segment-anchored` (the build's phases sit at their measured segment times), `t=0 allocation` (the technique's lifecycle is re-based to the build's own zero, with the re-basing named as an allocation), or `two-act` (a measured-window act plus a labeled allocation-model act) — and the item's build-record carries the same line. A Plan whose window-scope line lacks the schedule basis is incomplete in the same way a Plan lacking its swap values is (jev-plan-exit prices it). Landed by Cycle 013's Condense under the pattern rule; HQ may amend or retire it, and until then it is operative instruction, not candidacy.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:107:## Amendment A9 (2026-11-16, Cycle 023 Condense — the five Cycle-022 NOT-YET-AMENDED landings, plus this cycle's pattern promotion)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:112:4. **Raw-output filing (A9.4).** Build-records file the raw harness output (swap test, purity grep, syntax check) from the first draft, not a summary of it; a build-record whose own-checks section carries claims without the raw output beneath them is an ASSERTED-CHECKS defect at jev-prewave.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:116:## Amendment A10 (2026-11-17, Cycle 026 Condense — the three bundled restatements whose named consumer was this Condense)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:122:## Amendment A11 (2026-11-17, Cycle 028 Condense — census-checkpoint assertions; adopting the practice job's census-checkpoint note, practice Cycle 019 Condense, carried as a candidate by Cycle 027 §9.1 and adopted here on three independent demonstrations)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:123:Every item maps each Observe census checkpoint to an executable own-check assertion and its CONFIG-derived evaluation instant. The build-record identifies the checkpoint, the assertion, the CONFIG expression, and the evaluated result. jev-prewave returns ASSERTED-CHECKS if any checkpoint lacks this mapping, any evaluation instant uses hardcoded defaults, or execution evidence is absent. A CONFIG timing swap must move the corresponding assertion's evaluation instant. Demonstrations: practice T153 (timing 45→92) + T162 (timing 64→96), practice Cycle 019 · recreation Wave 25, all four items (timing lenses 92/96/96/100, no timing-stuck item, against Wave 22's allocation-vs-census timing failures at 68/64). Enforcement lives in jev-prewave.md §2 leg (3), amended in the same landing.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:125:## Amendment A12 (2026-11-18, Cycle 035 Condense — the ASSERTED-CHECKS pattern: T190 · T192 · T196 · T197 prewave HOLDs in one wave; T195's cure path as the positive demonstration)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:126:1. **Receipt form (operative step: §5 leg 3b's readiness check, referenced from §3 step 4).** Every A11 assertion in a build-record files its EXECUTABLE RECEIPT beside the claim — the harness command or run, the CONFIG expression evaluated, and the raw result from the build under review; for a CONFIG timing swap the receipt shows the changed evaluation instant. A9.4 already required raw output; this clause names the receipt's three parts and wires the check into the prewave step itself. A build-record whose assertions carry claims without receipts is incomplete at the builder's own gate: jev-prewave is not spent on it (the call's firing obligation is unchanged — the readiness check precedes payload assembly, and an unfired call still prints the cycle INCOMPLETE).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:130:## Amendment A13 (2026-11-18, Cycle 036 Condense — the receipt-completeness pattern: T190 · T196 · T197 · T199 prewave HOLDs in one wave; T192's 1.0-clearance as the positive demonstration; re-encoded under codex-condense REVISE before landing)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:131:1. **Receipt index + reconciliation (operative step: §5 leg 3b's readiness check, extended in the same landing).** Every build-record carries a RECEIPT INDEX enumerating (a) every guards.md command applicable to the item (1 purity · 2 swap · 3 syntax + seeded-RNG census · 4 arithmetic, seat-side · 5 segment binding · 6 fit leg · 7 census leg · 8 census-anchor probes where a zero-state anchor stands) and (b) every A11 assertion for the item. Readiness REQUIRES the reconciliation, not just the index: against the applicable guard commands, the item's planned A11 assertions, and — for a completion or re-attempt — the assertion sets established in the filed prior harnesses and their amendments; census receipts reconcile against the build's expected CONFIG keys (nested/array keys included — founding miss: T190's `scenes[].id` row). Every line carries its executable receipt or an explicit NOT-DEMANDED line whose disposition cites the governing plan or guard; a missing expected line, an unsupported exclusion, or a line with neither is incomplete at the builder's own gate: jev-prewave is not spent on it (the firing obligation is unchanged — the readiness check precedes payload assembly, per A12.1's form).
