- **Complete the CONFIG defaults.** Give explicit defaults for column positions, board top, ratio label offsets, arrow curvature, and annotation onset. Bind count-up easing separately from duration with the stated linear default. Specify supported count and spacing bounds for the reserved board and ratio derivation. (§§O3, P1, P6, P9 R3; gap G2.)
- **Complete the Verify instruments.** Add the recreation’s loaded-asset inventory and the exact checkpoint expressions that the harness will evaluate. Make the one- and three-column swap fixtures executable by specifying the replacement columns’ events and layout inputs or their derivation rules. (§§P4–P5, P9 R3; `INSTRUCTION.md` §5.2.)
- **Account for the entrance transition.** §O2 identifies an entrance transition at 84.5–85.5 s. §P9 R5 accounts for the opening handle, while R2 gives Texas an entrance instant without transition behavior. Specify the transition and duration or record the reduction and its reason. (§§O2, P2, P9 R2 and R5.)

**Limits** — This judgment uses the filed census descriptions and Plan. Source pixels and runtime behavior were not independently checked.

**BODY-WRITE: none (read-only run). T208’s verdict, scores, and amendment charges are for `RUN.md` §2b.**
